 36CA c  Identification of the first excited state in {+36}Ca.                  
 36CA c  2007Do11: {+36}Ca ions were produced via two-step fragmentation        
 36CA2c  technique, using the FRS-RISING setup at GSI. Primary {+40}Ca beam at  
 36CA3c  420 MeV/nucleon impinged a {+9}Be target. The {+37}Ca fragments were   
 36CA4c  selected on the basis of energy loss, magnetic rigidity and            
 36CA5c  time-of-flight. The {+37}Ca ions at an energy of 196 MeV/nucleon hit   
 36CA6c  a second {+9}Be target. The reaction products were selected using      
 36CA7c  calorimeter telescope array (CATE) of Si-CsI(Tl) modular               
 36CA8c  |DE-E telescopes. One-neutron knockout reaction from {+37}Ca           
 36CA c  2007Do11: Measured E|g, particle-|g coin, using 15 Cluster Ge detectors
 36CA2c  with seven elements in each cluster, seven six-fold MINIBALL triple Ge 
 36CA3c  detectors, and the HECTOR array of eight large-volume BaF{-2}          
 36CA4c  detectors. Fragment trajectories were determined using the CATE        
 36CA5c  array, and a thin Si |dE detector. The |g-ray spectra were             
 36CA6c  Doppler-corrected using Monte Carlo simulation GEANT4, corrected for   
 36CA7c  fragmentation of the primary beam using time-of-flight information.    
 36CA c  2007Bu15: {+36}Ca ions were produced via two-step fragmentation        
 36CA2c  technique, using GANIL facility. Primary {+40}Ca beam at               
 36CA3c  95 MeV/nucleon impinged a carbon target. The {+37}Ca fragments were    
 36CA4c  selected on the basis of energy loss, magnetic rigidity and            
 36CA5c  time-of-flight using |a spectrometer at GANIL. The {+37}Ca ions at     
 36CA6c  an energy of 45 MeV/nucleon hit a {+9}Be target. The {+36}Ca fragments 
 36CA7c  were selected using SPEG spectrometer at GANIL. One-neutron knockout   
 36CA8c  reaction from {+37}Ca. Measured |g rays using an array of 74 BaF{-2}   
 36CA9c  detectors. The |g-ray spectra were Doppler corrected. 2007Bu36         
